00:00:00.260 --> 00:00:00.470 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  the loki finale just blew up the mcu  we are now in full-on multiverse  territory as teams in avengers end game  and one division  eager marvel fans have long expected  this with spider-man no way home  dr strange in the multiverse of madness  and ant-man and the wasp quantomania  guaranteeing that we'll be seeing some  major timeline shenanigans in  mcu phase 4. loki however has finally  shown us how the multiverse can exist  in the finale we finally meet he who  remains a godlike figure who we discover  created the tva and is a true protector  of the sacred timeline  this timeline is destroyed though when  sylvie driven by revenge for being taken  by the tva as a child  kills he who remains creating endless  branches and truly cracking the  multiverse  wide open he who remains as played by  the enormously talented jonathan mages  it was first reported by deadline in  september 2020  that mages was cast as iconic marvel  villain kang the conqueror  and would be appearing in ant-man and  the wasp quantomania  in the comics he who remains and kang  the conqueror are different characters  but the mcu has merged the two as anyone  who saw the episode could attest  mage's performance as kang and loki was  certainly seen stealing and his previous  performances are equally as captivating  we just crossed the threshold  audiences likely know majors best from  his work on hbo's lovecraft country  based on the novel of the same name by  matt ruff mages plays atius freeman  a young man traveling 1950s america in  search of his missing father  not only does atticus have to overcome  the fierce racism in jim crow era  america  but some terrifying monsters said to  have inspired the iconic hp lovecraft  novels  lovecraft country was cancelled by hbo  but earned an impressive 18 nominations  at the 2021 emmys including outstanding  drama series  and outstanding lead actor for mages in  a statement responding to the  nominations as reported by indiewire  major said  thank you for seeing the light in the  dark and the smile and the tears of this  character  atticus freeman he is one of my best  friends and i'm glad you all got to meet  him as well  playing this role has changed my life  and this nomination is yet  another growing and changing moment  lovecraft country may have been mage's  breakout role but the performer has  shown his talents before  mages also starred in the 2017 abc  miniseries when we rise  a chronicled retelling of the gay rights  movement in the united states  mages portrays a young version of real  life lgbtq activist  ken jones an early advocate in  preventing the spread of hiv  particularly among gay black men on  playing such an important figure in the  gay rights movement  mages told w magazine my politics have  become very clear  and they've come to the surface of who i  am as a human being it's so rare to do a  piece where you don't have to separate  your politics and your work and your art  mages has also been praised for his work  in the a24 film  the last black man in san francisco  another overtly political project the  film follows a young black man's efforts  to reclaim his childhood home in gender  fried san francisco  written by and starring jimmy fails it's  a semi-autobiographical recount of  fail's own quest  to overcome the devastating impacts of  gentrification  major stars as montgomery allen bale's  best friend  the characters bond as a key component  of the story and talking with the  hollywood reporter  major shared that the actors connected  off-screen too mages told the outlet  there were deep things that were going  on in phil's life that we would just sit  and have breakfast and talk about  things that i've experienced what it is  to be young gifted and black or in my  case  young kind of gifted and black issues of  trying to be a young man in the world  he's my buddy he's my best friend the  last black man in san francisco  premiered at the 2019  sundance film festival and earned  director joe talbert both the u.s  dramatic directing award  and a special drawing award barack obama  also named it as one of his favorite  films of 2019  audiences may also know mages from his  work on white boy rick  starring matthew mcconaughey and set in  1980s detroit at the height of the war  on drugs the film follows a blue-collar  father  and his teenage son rick based on a true  story  rick becomes the fbi's youngest ever  drug informant at age 14  and quickly finds himself immersed in  the lucrative world of drug dealing  major stars as johnny curry a local  kingpin who brings rick into his fold of  illegal activities  the actor talked to the source about how  he hopes the film would challenge  people's perception of drug dealers  calling his character a leader of men he  elaborated  saying that's something we miss when  we're dealing with african-american drug  dealers it's an occupation he could be a  lawyer or doctor and have the same  attributes it's just the fact that he's  a drug dealer it's easy to write him off  with his career still in its early  stages and already having a slew of  impressive roles behind him  jonathan mages is ready for more success  the ending of the first loki season is  just one sign of greater things to come  for him  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  your favorite mcu actors are coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss  a single one

